+# Draft mapping from current records to `schema.sql`
+
+All counts below are from `python3 scripts/inventory.py > inventory.jsonl` on 30 Oct 2026. Field occurrence counts and types for every source are in `RECORDS.csv`; `inventory.jsonl` retains the machine-readable measurement. The files are live, so a migration must take a new read-only snapshot and re-count. Every imported JSON row also goes to `source_records` or a table's `raw_json` field with source path, line/index, and content SHA so old fields are not lost.
+
+| Current source | Observed rows | Destination and key | Migration rule / fidelity |
+|---|---:|---|---|
+| `registry/tasks.json` | 34 tasks | `tasks.slug`; `stage_history(slug, changed_at, to_stage, source_sha)` | Copy full task/pipeline JSON. Current pipeline has `stage` 34/34, `stage_since` only 10/34; seed one `stage_history` row per current task marked `snapshot`, with earlier transitions **UNVERIFIED**. Do not invent history. |
+| `board.json` | 352 rows | `sessions.sha` | Copy every row, including `kind` (209/352) and `pending_id`; preserve exact `step` and result path. If a referenced pending ID is absent, import with NULL FK and retain original in `board_json`, then report discrepancy. |
+| `pending.db` | 457 `items`, 1,249 `history` | `pending_items.id`; `pending_history.source_rowid` | Read using SQLite `mode=ro`, copy every column and history `rowid` in one consistent read transaction. Preserve ID format. `tools/pending.py:37-49` defines schema. |
+| `registry/scores.jsonl` | 112 lines | `runs(source_path, source_ordinal)` | Preserve each heterogeneous row; extract `slug`, `event`, `tree_sha`, `rewards.tests/rubric/combined` when present. Only 49 rows have `rewards`; `valid` exists in 45, so missing validity is NULL, not true. Legacy non-run analysis rows stay in `source_records` with optional `runs` row only when classifiable. |
+| Harness `.master-queue/state.json` | 92 runs, 0 queued | `queue_runs(task, attempt, source_path)` | Snapshot score/status/job fields as external operational history. The harness queue keeps owning and locking its live state (`scripts/master_queue.py:148-164`); DB is a read model. |
+| `QC/reports/*/result_*.json` | 86 files | `qc_rounds.sha` plus `session_results.sha` | Copy `fail/minor/warn`, `kit`, report path, rewards and QL counts; full result JSON retained. Link only if SHA exists on board; otherwise flag orphan. Worker schema is at `prompts/templates/P11_full_qc_v3.md:105`. |
+| QC `v*.md` reports | file count **UNVERIFIED** | `qc_findings(qc_sha,finding_id)` | Keep report path and content hash. Parse finding IDs/severity/evidence only where a stable ID is present; do not convert aggregate count into invented findings. Manual review of unparsed reports before treating `qc_findings` as complete. |
+| `decisions.jsonl` | 589 lines | `decisions(source_path, source_line)` | Preserve all raw rows. Legacy `who/decision/verbatim` and newer `by/what/words` map to actor/text/verbatim; observed `by` 229, `who` 336, `decision` 577, `what` 11. No lossy rewrite. |
+| `feedback.jsonl` | 26 lines | `feedback(source_path, source_line)` | Preserve full row; `verbatim` 19, `class` 23, `action` 11. |
+| `lessons.jsonl` | 88 lines | `lessons(source_path, source_line)` | Preserve full row; `lesson` 88, `kind` 21, `status` 67. |
+| `registry/levers.json` | 68 levers | `levers.lever_id`; `task_levers` | Preserve full lever JSON; populate task link only from unambiguous task IDs/slug references. |
+| `registry/ideas.jsonl` | 5 lines | `ideas(source_path,source_line)` | Preserve full row and verdict. |
+| `registry/peer_tasks.json` | 20 tasks | `peer_tasks.slug` | Preserve full evidence, repository head and verdict. |
+| `open_questions.json` | 17 open, 19 closed | `questions.id` | Historical import; README calls it retired (`README.md:57`). Detect duplicate IDs or state conflicts before merge. |
+| `state.json` | one config object | `meta` or versioned source record | Keep standing rules/config under versioned keys; this is not live task status (`README.md:11,45`). Do not let a worker modify it through inbox. |
+| `log.jsonl` | 169 lines | `source_records` (optional event projection) | Historical import only; retired per `README.md:57`. |
+| `auto/runs/*/state.json` | 10 files | `auto_runs.run_dir` | Preserve each run's full state; operational file remains auto-owned. |
+| `auto/runs/*/events.jsonl` | 308 lines in 9 files | `auto_events(run_dir,line_no)` | Preserve append order and raw JSON; one older run uses `night_log.jsonl` (43 lines), same destination with source path in `run_dir` namespace. |
+| Worker `result_<sha>.json` | 108 board paths parse as JSON | `session_results.sha` | `scripts/results_inventory.py` found 107 matching SHA, 1 mismatch; board has 94 directory paths, 6 Markdown paths, and 144 missing paths. Import only verified matching JSON, preserve other paths and report the mismatch. The 86 QC results overlap this inventory. |
+
+## Migration ordering and validation
+
+1. Freeze a *read-only snapshot* by copying source bytes into a migration staging folder while the master pauses its own writes. The harness and workers may continue, but mark their snapshot cutoff and replay new inbox/event records later. Hash every source. A file that changes during the copy is retried; no source is edited.
+2. Import pending, tasks, board, levers, then scores, QC results, decisions, feedback, lessons, auto and queue snapshots, and historical records into a **new** DB. FK failures, duplicate keys, malformed JSON, and source drift are listed before any cutover. Stage/history records inferred from a current snapshot are labelled as such.
+3. Dry run `PRAGMA foreign_key_check; PRAGMA integrity_check;` and compare counts: tasks 34, sessions 352, pending items 457/history 1,249, decisions 589, feedback 26, lessons 88, levers 68, ideas 5, peer tasks 20, auto state 10, auto events 308 plus night 43, queue runs 92, QC results 86. Scores must account for all 112 raw lines even if fewer become typed `runs`. Recompute counts at cutover; these are example baseline values, not fixed assertions.
+4. Compare current `status.py` output, pending list, `BOARD.md`, latest valid score per task, and QC round counts to DB-generated views. Manually resolve the one observed board-result SHA mismatch and all orphan QC results before declaring equivalence.
+5. Switch read paths first. Keep old files intact as rollback and archive inputs. Switch master writes only after a shadow period with zero count/view differences. Generate `BOARD.md` and a compact `STATUS.md` from one DB snapshot; keep `status.py` as a CLI facade. Human-readable views remain generated artifacts, not competing truth.
+
+## Safety and rollback
+
+One master process owns all DB writes. Use SQLite WAL, `busy_timeout=5000`, `foreign_keys=ON`, one short `BEGIN IMMEDIATE` transaction per merge, and `synchronous=FULL` for the authoritative DB. Readers use `mode=ro` and never create tables. Use SQLite's backup API (WAL-consistent snapshot) before migration/cutover, before schema upgrades, and once daily after the final merge; store under `master_chat_tasks/backups/` with timestamp and SHA manifest, keep 14 daily and 4 weekly copies. Verify each with `quick_check` and an open/restore rehearsal. Do not copy only the `.sqlite` file while WAL is active. On failed migration, delete only the new staging DB and continue on existing files. On failed cutover, stop DB writes, restore the last verified backup to a new path, replay retained inboxes by SHA, compare counts/views, and point the master back to the old file workflow until differences are resolved. No rollback deletes worker inbox or original result files.
diff --git a/schema.sql b/schema.sql
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..26170c2cbda6467d7490af0849b77b362ad3e184
--- /dev/null
+++ b/schema.sql
@@ -0,0 +1,170 @@
+-- DRAFT ONLY. Proposed path: master_chat_tasks/pipeline.sqlite.
+-- Apply only after an explicit migration plan and Ayush's build approval.
+PRAGMA foreign_keys = ON;
+PRAGMA busy_timeout = 5000;
+PRAGMA journal_mode = WAL;
+
+BEGIN IMMEDIATE;
+CREATE TABLE meta (key TEXT PRIMARY KEY, value TEXT NOT NULL);
+CREATE TABLE source_records (
+  source_path TEXT NOT NULL, source_ordinal TEXT NOT NULL,
+  content_sha256 TEXT NOT NULL, raw_json TEXT NOT NULL CHECK(json_valid(raw_json)),
+  imported_at TEXT NOT NULL, PRIMARY KEY(source_path, source_ordinal)
+);
+CREATE INDEX source_records_hash ON source_records(content_sha256);
+
+CREATE TABLE tasks (
+  slug TEXT PRIMARY KEY, stage TEXT, stage_since TEXT, kind TEXT, tree_sha TEXT,
+  next_action TEXT, updated_at TEXT, pipeline_json TEXT NOT NULL CHECK(json_valid(pipeline_json)),
+  task_json TEXT NOT NULL CHECK(json_valid(task_json))
+);
+CREATE INDEX tasks_stage ON tasks(stage, updated_at);
+CREATE TABLE stage_history (
+  id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, slug TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES tasks(slug),
+  from_stage TEXT, to_stage TEXT NOT NULL, changed_at TEXT NOT NULL,
+  source_sha TEXT, reason TEXT, source_record TEXT,
+  UNIQUE(slug, changed_at, to_stage, source_sha)
+);
+CREATE INDEX stage_history_task_time ON stage_history(slug, changed_at DESC);
+
+CREATE TABLE pending_items (
+  id TEXT PRIMARY KEY, kind TEXT NOT NULL, title TEXT NOT NULL,
+  detail TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT '', prompt TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT '', send_back TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT '',
+  seq INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 100, priority TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'medium',
+  status TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'open', owner TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'Ayush', note TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT '',
+  created_ist TEXT, updated_ist TEXT, closed_ist TEXT
+);
+CREATE INDEX pending_open_order ON pending_items(status, seq, id);
+CREATE TABLE pending_history (
+  id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, item_id TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES pending_items(id),
+  source_rowid INTEGER UNIQUE, ist TEXT, change_text TEXT NOT NULL
+);
+CREATE INDEX pending_history_item ON pending_history(item_id, id);
+
+CREATE TABLE sessions (
+  sha TEXT PRIMARY KEY CHECK(length(sha)=7), slug TEXT NOT NULL,
+  step TEXT NOT NULL, kind TEXT, prompt_path TEXT NOT NULL, result_path TEXT NOT NULL,
+  status TEXT NOT NULL, pending_id TEXT REFERENCES pending_items(id),
+  issued_at TEXT NOT NULL, started_at TEXT, updated_at TEXT, note TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT '',
+  board_json TEXT NOT NULL CHECK(json_valid(board_json))
+);
+CREATE INDEX sessions_slug_time ON sessions(slug, issued_at DESC);
+CREATE INDEX sessions_status_time ON sessions(status, issued_at DESC);
+CREATE TABLE session_results (
+  sha TEXT PRIMARY KEY REFERENCES sessions(sha), payload_sha256 TEXT NOT NULL,
+  status TEXT, verdict TEXT, report_path TEXT, result_json TEXT NOT NULL CHECK(json_valid(result_json)),
+  imported_at TEXT NOT NULL
+);
+CREATE TABLE inbox_merges (
+  sha TEXT PRIMARY KEY REFERENCES sessions(sha), schema_version INTEGER NOT NULL,
+  inbox_path TEXT NOT NULL, file_sha256 TEXT NOT NULL, result_sha256 TEXT NOT NULL,
+  merged_at TEXT NOT NULL, outcome TEXT NOT NULL CHECK(outcome IN ('applied','partial','blocked'))
+);
+CREATE TABLE inbox_conflicts (
+  id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, sha TEXT NOT NULL, inbox_path TEXT NOT NULL,
+  file_sha256 TEXT NOT NULL, observed_at TEXT NOT NULL, reason TEXT NOT NULL,
+  resolution TEXT, resolved_at TEXT
+);
+CREATE INDEX inbox_conflicts_sha ON inbox_conflicts(sha, observed_at DESC);
+
+CREATE TABLE runs (
+  id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, slug TEXT NOT NULL, event TEXT NOT NULL,
+  session_sha TEXT REFERENCES sessions(sha), source_path TEXT NOT NULL,
+  source_ordinal TEXT NOT NULL, tree_sha TEXT, report_path TEXT, valid INTEGER,
+  artefact_reason TEXT, happened_at TEXT, tests REAL, rubric REAL, combined REAL,
+  run_json TEXT NOT NULL CHECK(json_valid(run_json)),
+  UNIQUE(source_path, source_ordinal)
+);
+CREATE INDEX runs_task_time ON runs(slug, happened_at DESC);
+CREATE INDEX runs_valid_event ON runs(valid, event, happened_at DESC);
+CREATE TABLE queue_runs (
+  task TEXT NOT NULL, attempt INTEGER NOT NULL, source_path TEXT NOT NULL,
+  status TEXT, started_at TEXT, finished_at TEXT, job_dir TEXT, route TEXT,
+  run_json TEXT NOT NULL CHECK(json_valid(run_json)),
+  PRIMARY KEY(task, attempt, source_path)
+);
+
+CREATE TABLE qc_rounds (
+  sha TEXT PRIMARY KEY REFERENCES sessions(sha), slug TEXT NOT NULL,
+  mode TEXT, status TEXT, verdict TEXT, report_path TEXT NOT NULL,
+  fail_count INTEGER, minor_count INTEGER, warn_count INTEGER,
+  kit_sha TEXT, rewards_json TEXT CHECK(rewards_json IS NULL OR json_valid(rewards_json)),
+  ql_rows_json TEXT CHECK(ql_rows_json IS NULL OR json_valid(ql_rows_json)),
+  result_json TEXT NOT NULL CHECK(json_valid(result_json))
+);
+CREATE INDEX qc_rounds_task ON qc_rounds(slug, sha);
+CREATE TABLE qc_findings (
+  id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, qc_sha TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES qc_rounds(sha),
+  finding_id TEXT, severity TEXT, title TEXT, evidence TEXT,
+  ruling TEXT, report_line INTEGER, raw_text TEXT,
+  UNIQUE(qc_sha, finding_id)
+);
+CREATE INDEX qc_findings_round_severity ON qc_findings(qc_sha, severity);
+
+CREATE TABLE decisions (
+  id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, source_path TEXT NOT NULL, source_line INTEGER NOT NULL,
+  ist TEXT, actor TEXT, slug TEXT, decision_text TEXT, verbatim TEXT,
+  raw_json TEXT NOT NULL CHECK(json_valid(raw_json)), UNIQUE(source_path,source_line)
+);
+CREATE INDEX decisions_task_time ON decisions(slug, ist DESC);
+CREATE TABLE feedback (
+  id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, source_path TEXT NOT NULL, source_line INTEGER NOT NULL,
+  ist TEXT, actor TEXT, class TEXT, verbatim TEXT, action TEXT,
+  raw_json TEXT NOT NULL CHECK(json_valid(raw_json)), UNIQUE(source_path,source_line)
+);
+CREATE TABLE lessons (
+  id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, source_path TEXT NOT NULL, source_line INTEGER NOT NULL,
+  ist TEXT, kind TEXT, lesson TEXT, status TEXT,
+  raw_json TEXT NOT NULL CHECK(json_valid(raw_json)), UNIQUE(source_path,source_line)
+);
+CREATE TABLE levers (
+  lever_id TEXT PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL, family TEXT, status TEXT,
+  first_task TEXT, lever_json TEXT NOT NULL CHECK(json_valid(lever_json))
+);
+CREATE INDEX levers_status_family ON levers(status, family);
+CREATE TABLE task_levers (
+  slug TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES tasks(slug), lever_id TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES levers(lever_id),
+  source TEXT, PRIMARY KEY(slug, lever_id)
+);
+CREATE TABLE exceptions (
+  id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, slug TEXT, scope TEXT NOT NULL, rule TEXT NOT NULL,
+  permitted_by TEXT NOT NULL, verbatim TEXT, decision_id INTEGER REFERENCES decisions(id),
+  valid_from TEXT, valid_until TEXT, active INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 1,
+  evidence_path TEXT, raw_json TEXT CHECK(raw_json IS NULL OR json_valid(raw_json))
+);
+CREATE INDEX exceptions_task_active ON exceptions(slug, active);
+
+CREATE TABLE ideas (
+  id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, source_path TEXT NOT NULL, source_line INTEGER NOT NULL,
+  idea_id TEXT, verdict TEXT, raw_json TEXT NOT NULL CHECK(json_valid(raw_json)),
+  UNIQUE(source_path,source_line)
+);
+CREATE TABLE peer_tasks (
+  slug TEXT PRIMARY KEY, verdict TEXT, repo_head TEXT,
+  raw_json TEXT NOT NULL CHECK(json_valid(raw_json))
+);
+CREATE TABLE questions (
+  id TEXT PRIMARY KEY, status TEXT, owner TEXT, asked_ist TEXT,
+  closed_ist TEXT, question TEXT, answer TEXT, raw_json TEXT NOT NULL CHECK(json_valid(raw_json))
+);
+CREATE TABLE auto_runs (
+  run_dir TEXT PRIMARY KEY, label TEXT, started TEXT, ended TEXT,
+  state_json TEXT NOT NULL CHECK(json_valid(state_json))
+);
+CREATE TABLE auto_events (
+  run_dir TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES auto_runs(run_dir), line_no INTEGER NOT NULL,
+  ist TEXT, event TEXT, sha TEXT, raw_json TEXT NOT NULL CHECK(json_valid(raw_json)),
+  PRIMARY KEY(run_dir,line_no)
+);
+CREATE INDEX auto_events_sha_time ON auto_events(sha,ist);
+
+CREATE VIEW active_sessions AS
+  SELECT sha, slug, step, status, pending_id, issued_at, prompt_path, result_path
+  FROM sessions WHERE status IN ('issued','running') ORDER BY issued_at DESC;
+CREATE VIEW task_status AS
+  SELECT t.slug,t.stage,t.kind,t.tree_sha,t.next_action,
+    (SELECT r.tests FROM runs r WHERE r.slug=t.slug AND r.valid=1 ORDER BY r.happened_at DESC,r.id DESC LIMIT 1) AS latest_tests,
+    (SELECT r.rubric FROM runs r WHERE r.slug=t.slug AND r.valid=1 ORDER BY r.happened_at DESC,r.id DESC LIMIT 1) AS latest_rubric,
+    (SELECT r.combined FROM runs r WHERE r.slug=t.slug AND r.valid=1 ORDER BY r.happened_at DESC,r.id DESC LIMIT 1) AS latest_combined
+  FROM tasks t;
+COMMIT;
