+# Draft mapping from current records to `schema.sql`
+
+All counts below are from `python3 scripts/inventory.py > inventory.jsonl` on 30 Oct 2026. Field occurrence counts and types for every source are in `RECORDS.csv`; `inventory.jsonl` retains the machine-readable measurement. The files are live, so a migration must take a new read-only snapshot and re-count. Every imported JSON row also goes to `source_records` or a table's `raw_json` field with source path, line/index, and content SHA so old fields are not lost.
+
+| Current source | Observed rows | Destination and key | Migration rule / fidelity |
+|---|---:|---|---|
+| `registry/tasks.json` | 34 tasks | `tasks.slug`; `stage_history(slug, changed_at, to_stage, source_sha)` | Copy full task/pipeline JSON. Current pipeline has `stage` 34/34, `stage_since` only 10/34; seed one `stage_history` row per current task marked `snapshot`, with earlier transitions **UNVERIFIED**. Do not invent history. |
+| `board.json` | 352 rows | `sessions.sha` | Copy every row, including `kind` (209/352) and `pending_id`; preserve exact `step` and result path. If a referenced pending ID is absent, import with NULL FK and retain original in `board_json`, then report discrepancy. |
+| `pending.db` | 457 `items`, 1,249 `history` | `pending_items.id`; `pending_history.source_rowid` | Read using SQLite `mode=ro`, copy every column and history `rowid` in one consistent read transaction. Preserve ID format. `tools/pending.py:37-49` defines schema. |
+| `registry/scores.jsonl` | 112 lines | `runs(source_path, source_ordinal)` | Preserve each heterogeneous row; extract `slug`, `event`, `tree_sha`, `rewards.tests/rubric/combined` when present. Only 49 rows have `rewards`; `valid` exists in 45, so missing validity is NULL, not true. Legacy non-run analysis rows stay in `source_records` with optional `runs` row only when classifiable. |
+| Harness `.master-queue/state.json` | 92 runs, 0 queued | `queue_runs(task, attempt, source_path)` | Snapshot score/status/job fields as external operational history. The harness queue keeps owning and locking its live state (`scripts/master_queue.py:148-164`); DB is a read model. |
+| `QC/reports/*/result_*.json` | 86 files | `qc_rounds.sha` plus `session_results.sha` | Copy `fail/minor/warn`, `kit`, report path, rewards and QL counts; full result JSON retained. Link only if SHA exists on board; otherwise flag orphan. Worker schema is at `prompts/templates/P11_full_qc_v3.md:105`. |
+| QC `v*.md` reports | file count **UNVERIFIED** | `qc_findings(qc_sha,finding_id)` | Keep report path and content hash. Parse finding IDs/severity/evidence only where a stable ID is present; do not convert aggregate count into invented findings. Manual review of unparsed reports before treating `qc_findings` as complete. |
+| `decisions.jsonl` | 589 lines | `decisions(source_path, source_line)` | Preserve all raw rows. Legacy `who/decision/verbatim` and newer `by/what/words` map to actor/text/verbatim; observed `by` 229, `who` 336, `decision` 577, `what` 11. No lossy rewrite. |
+| `feedback.jsonl` | 26 lines | `feedback(source_path, source_line)` | Preserve full row; `verbatim` 19, `class` 23, `action` 11. |
+| `lessons.jsonl` | 88 lines | `lessons(source_path, source_line)` | Preserve full row; `lesson` 88, `kind` 21, `status` 67. |
+| `registry/levers.json` | 68 levers | `levers.lever_id`; `task_levers` | Preserve full lever JSON; populate task link only from unambiguous task IDs/slug references. |
+| `registry/ideas.jsonl` | 5 lines | `ideas(source_path,source_line)` | Preserve full row and verdict. |
+| `registry/peer_tasks.json` | 20 tasks | `peer_tasks.slug` | Preserve full evidence, repository head and verdict. |
+| `open_questions.json` | 17 open, 19 closed | `questions.id` | Historical import; README calls it retired (`README.md:57`). Detect duplicate IDs or state conflicts before merge. |
+| `state.json` | one config object | `meta` or versioned source record | Keep standing rules/config under versioned keys; this is not live task status (`README.md:11,45`). Do not let a worker modify it through inbox. |
+| `log.jsonl` | 169 lines | `source_records` (optional event projection) | Historical import only; retired per `README.md:57`. |
+| `auto/runs/*/state.json` | 10 files | `auto_runs.run_dir` | Preserve each run's full state; operational file remains auto-owned. |
+| `auto/runs/*/events.jsonl` | 308 lines in 9 files | `auto_events(run_dir,line_no)` | Preserve append order and raw JSON; one older run uses `night_log.jsonl` (43 lines), same destination with source path in `run_dir` namespace. |
+| Worker `result_<sha>.json` | 108 board paths parse as JSON | `session_results.sha` | `scripts/results_inventory.py` found 107 matching SHA, 1 mismatch; board has 94 directory paths, 6 Markdown paths, and 144 missing paths. Import only verified matching JSON, preserve other paths and report the mismatch. The 86 QC results overlap this inventory. |
+
+## Migration ordering and validation
+
+1. Freeze a *read-only snapshot* by copying source bytes into a migration staging folder while the master pauses its own writes. The harness and workers may continue, but mark their snapshot cutoff and replay new inbox/event records later. Hash every source. A file that changes during the copy is retried; no source is edited.
+2. Import pending, tasks, board, levers, then scores, QC results, decisions, feedback, lessons, auto and queue snapshots, and historical records into a **new** DB. FK failures, duplicate keys, malformed JSON, and source drift are listed before any cutover. Stage/history records inferred from a current snapshot are labelled as such.
+3. Dry run `PRAGMA foreign_key_check; PRAGMA integrity_check;` and compare counts: tasks 34, sessions 352, pending items 457/history 1,249, decisions 589, feedback 26, lessons 88, levers 68, ideas 5, peer tasks 20, auto state 10, auto events 308 plus night 43, queue runs 92, QC results 86. Scores must account for all 112 raw lines even if fewer become typed `runs`. Recompute counts at cutover; these are example baseline values, not fixed assertions.
+4. Compare current `status.py` output, pending list, `BOARD.md`, latest valid score per task, and QC round counts to DB-generated views. Manually resolve the one observed board-result SHA mismatch and all orphan QC results before declaring equivalence.
+5. Switch read paths first. Keep old files intact as rollback and archive inputs. Switch master writes only after a shadow period with zero count/view differences. Generate `BOARD.md` and a compact `STATUS.md` from one DB snapshot; keep `status.py` as a CLI facade. Human-readable views remain generated artifacts, not competing truth.
+
+## Safety and rollback
+
+One master process owns all DB writes. Use SQLite WAL, `busy_timeout=5000`, `foreign_keys=ON`, one short `BEGIN IMMEDIATE` transaction per merge, and `synchronous=FULL` for the authoritative DB. Readers use `mode=ro` and never create tables. Use SQLite's backup API (WAL-consistent snapshot) before migration/cutover, before schema upgrades, and once daily after the final merge; store under `master_chat_tasks/backups/` with timestamp and SHA manifest, keep 14 daily and 4 weekly copies. Verify each with `quick_check` and an open/restore rehearsal. Do not copy only the `.sqlite` file while WAL is active. On failed migration, delete only the new staging DB and continue on existing files. On failed cutover, stop DB writes, restore the last verified backup to a new path, replay retained inboxes by SHA, compare counts/views, and point the master back to the old file workflow until differences are resolved. No rollback deletes worker inbox or original result files.
